sed on mary's body as the source of  christ's flesh the pregnancy of mary was  proof of christ's humanity  that said  mary's role was to be limited and was  not to redeem all women  the second century church father  tertullian for example  said once mary had contributed her flesh  in obedience to god's will her role was  done  after christ's birth tertullian wrote  mary became a wife including bearing  future children brothers of jesus  therefore she no longer held any  authority as a dedicated virgin  tertullian introduced the famous attack  on women  you are the devil's gateway through  which death entered the world  even ambrose  a great advocate of virginity warned of  excess veneration of mary he wrote  mary was the temple of god  not the god of the temple  so they walked a fine line between  respect for mary's role and not giving  her too much credit  it's not surprising that no churches  except in ephesus were dedicated to mary  before pulkaria's confrontation with  nestorius  mary's role  probably would have remained ambiguous  with people accepting a position  articulated by the priest  peter chrysologus in the 5th century  when he preached it was best not to pry  too much into this virgin's conceiving  but believe it  4 28 it was too late for that  the battle lines were drawn and pulkaria  was going to vindicate mary  and  herself for a few years after the  disastrous confrontation on easter  sunday the people of constantinople and  the court itself took sides  the emperor theodosius supported his  archbishop nestorius while plucario was  his implacable enemy  and she had acquired a champion of her  own  cyril bishop of alexandria  cyril had gotten into disputes with  nestorius earlier and was ready to gain  precarious support in this fight  finally theodosius called a council  the third ecumenical council to convene  in 431 to settle the question of whether  mary gave birth to god  although theodosius was sure the council  would vindicate nestorius he wan