age was to be a political one  of convenience only never consummated  marcion took over the armies of the  empire and left theology to bulgaria  in 451 at bulkaria's urging marcion  convened a council to meet in calcidon a  city near constantinople that today is a  suburb of istanbul she had enough  control in the capital that she didn't  need ephesus this time  when the council met in calcidon the  empress bulkaria appeared in person to  address the bishops who had traveled  from far away to attend  if nestorius had been shocked to see  bulkaria enter the sanctuary in her own  church  the bishops and council in calcidon must  have been even more shocked to see a  woman address the venerable body of  churchmen  she was too powerful for anyone to  object and not surprisingly the council  agreed with her position on the  incarnation  the virgin mary continued to be exalted  as the council stated a real body was  received from her body and christ  embodied both human and divine natures  fully  the churchmen and council went further  and praised bulgaria many years to the  empress you are the light of orthodoxy  because of this there will be peace  everywhere you have persecuted all  heresies  again not surprisingly everyone did not  agree with the formulation hammered out  at calcodon  those who believe the manger held an  infant that was fully god  left  the modern coptic church of egypt holds  this anti-calcidon position  but that was in the future  pulkaria celebrated her decisive  theological victory  how did pulkaria celebrate her  vindication of the virgin mary  she built churches and in this she  started the shift to a more visible  veneration of the virgin mary  she built three churches dedicated to  the mother of god in constantinople  ephesus would no longer be the only city  that had a church of the virgin  tradition attributes three shrines  calcoprotea blashanai and hodigetria to  bulkaria's foundation  however there was a problem  churches without relics 